# SM-T715 (Galaxy Tab S2 8.0 LTE, arm64 port) build of omarchy-mobile's
# omamobile-shell 0.2.133 for Omarchy 4.5, after the owner's other tablet port
# (Lenovomarchy, image/pkg/omamobile-shell 0.2.133-3, which runs on its tablet
# over Omarchy 4.5.0-3) with the SM-T715's own tablet patches carried forward
# from its 0.2.94 build (Omarchy 4.0.6).
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/derekross/omarchy-mobile, packages/
# omamobile-shell 0.2.133 at commit c4623572be1c141d602cf99a83ae0bf9e3eea09c,
# tarball checked by sha256 (GitHub's archive as served on 2026-11-24, top
# directory omamobile-<commit>; checked against the commit's git tree with
# tools/verify-github-archive, and identical in content to the encoding
# Lenovomarchy pins).
#
# What it is: ordinary Omarchy shell plugins (QML) that turn Omarchy's shell
# into a touch shell: a status bar with a pull-down quick-settings sheet
# (omamobile.bar replaces omarchy.bar), the dock, app drawer and search bar
# (omamobile.launcher), recent apps (omamobile.switcher), home screens
# (omamobile.home, built-in widgets only), the call card (omamobile.call),
# the keyboard's show/hide calls and language sheet (omamobile.keyboard),
# and the edge back swipe (omamobile.back); omamobile-setup-user links them
# into the user's config. Nothing here is compiled and nothing patches
# Hyprland (the image's rootfs/t715-tablet.lua has the window rules; upstream's
# hypr/phone.lua is not installed).
#
# The series (this directory; each patch's header says more):
#   0001 tablet-quick-settings-tiles  no torch, location, NFC or fingerprint
#        tiles (Mobile data comes back in 0010); Hotspot under "Add tiles";
#        Rotation in the default layout (Lenovomarchy's 0001, with the
#        SM-T715's tiles)
#   0002 tablet-wifi-wpa2-without-sae  WPA2-PSK for a WPA3/WPA2 SSID: the
#        BCM4358 firmware has no SAE (Lenovomarchy's 0002; the SM-T715's 0002)
#   0003 tablet-quiet-pollers  no do-not-disturb poll; the modem and call
#        watchers only when the profile asks (true in tablet-shell.json;
#        Lenovomarchy's 0003)
#   0004 tablet-phone-leftovers  no unshipped plugin, menu row or probe
#        (Lenovomarchy's 0004), with upstream's suspend-off step kept and its
#        tile-refresh guard fixed for the Rotation tile this build keeps;
#        omamobile.call is shipped again (the modem runs on arm64 now)
#   0005 tablet-rotate-tile  Rotate: a quarter turn by hand (t715-rotate)
#   0006 tablet-airplane-and-hotspot  Airplane mode through nmcli radio for
#        Wi-Fi and the modem; Hotspot shows its password
#   0007 tablet-set-pin  "tablet" wording; sudo asks once a PIN is set
#   0008 tablet-back-gesture  the swipe is the Back key's (t715-keys), with
#        upstream's Escape as the fallback
#   0009 tablet-sdcard-tile  the SD card tile over t715-sdcard
#   0010 tablet-modem  the Mobile data tile back, through NetworkManager's
#        gsm connection (t715-mobile); signal bars and technology from
#        shannonctl status (the SM-T715's 0.2.94 series' 0004)
#   0011 tablet-mobile-settings  the Mobile data tile's long press, or a tap
#        while no connection exists, opens t715-mobile-settings (the 0.2.94
#        series' 0006)
#   0012 tablet-modem-tile  the Modem tile over t715-modem-power; the Mobile
#        data tile says "Modem off" while it is off (the 0.2.94 series' 0011)
#   0013 tablet-call-card  no Speaker toggle on the call card (no earpiece;
#        the 0.2.94 series' 0007's call-card hunk)
# Not carried forward from the SM-T715's 0.2.94 series, for the arm64 image
# (the commands they drive are not in it): 0010 tablet-location-tile (no
# t715-gps) and 0013 tablet-android-tile (no Waydroid on the arm64 kernel
# yet). Upstream did what the 0.2.94 series' 0009 worked around (Escape by
# name): 0008 keeps upstream's fix as its fallback.
#
# The profiles: profile/shell.json is tablet-shell.json (only the plugins
# shipped here, the drawer at 6 columns, Omarchy's idle timers at 0 (off;
# t715-idle turns the screen off), the modem and call watchers on (the modem
# runs on arm64 now), the 18 bar-widget-only Omarchy plugins and
# omarchy.remote-session in disabledPlugins; omarchy.idle stays, as on the
# 0.2.94 build) and profile/home.json is tablet-home.json (Lenovomarchy's 6x8
# home grid with the image's apps).
#
# Dropped from upstream's install, as Lenovomarchy drops them (its PKGBUILD
# has every reason): the plugins omamobile.fingerprint, .update, .access,
# .voice, .mobilenetwork; the bins for fingerprint enrolment, NFC, the
# phone's keys, sleep and double-tap daemons, onboarding, the permission
# portal, intents, voice, weather, mobile network and the update sheet's
# reboot; hypr/phone.lua, squeekboard's layouts and their generator (the
# image ships its own terminal layouts with Esc), the keyboard theme hook,
# the OSK and fcitx5 environment files, the portal drop-ins, the desktop
# entries and omamobile-osk-guard. Not depended on: omamobile-apps (the
# dialer, SMS, NFC and maps), omamobile-omarchy (the image installs it
# anyway), omamobile-owl-widgets (off), omatel-agent (the image keeps it; the
# call plugin and both watchers ship again, 0004 and 0013).
#
# Build: tools/build-pkg omamobile-shell (rootfs/build.sh does it). Image:
# rootfs/install-mobile.sh, rootfs/omarchy-user-setup.sh; checks: the smoke
# check.

# Maintainer (upstream): Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>

pkgname=omamobile-shell
pkgver=0.2.133
pkgrel=4.1
pkgdesc="Omarchy Mobile's touch shell for Omarchy: status bar, quick settings, launcher, recents, home, back swipe (SM-T715 tablet build)"
arch=(any)
url="https://github.com/derekross/omarchy-mobile"
license=(MIT)
depends=(
  'omarchy>=4.0.6'
  bash python python-dbus python-gobject   # osk-watch, bt-agent, keyboard-languages, widget
  squeekboard                               # the on-screen keyboard (sm.puri.OSK0)
  quickshell                                # the host shell (qs); pulled by omarchy already
  qt6-declarative                           # the QML runtime the plugins import
  bluez bluez-utils                         # Bluetooth panel and rfkill
  networkmanager iw                         # Wi-Fi panel, the SAE probe (patch 0002)
  util-linux                                # busctl (keyboard tile), rfkill
  jq                                        # BackModel's terminal sniff, omamobile-launch
  inotify-tools                             # the home screen's user-widget watch
  wtype                                     # the back gesture's Escape (its fallback here)
  wf-recorder                               # the Screen record tile
  libnotify                                 # omamobile-screenrecord's fallback toast
  brightnessctl                             # the brightness slider
)
optdepends=(
  'loupe: what a screenshot toast opens (omamobile-screenshot-open); the image installs it'
  'khal: events in the home screen calendar widget'
  'playerctl: the home screen media widget'
  'power-profiles-daemon: the Battery saver tile (dimmed "No power profiles" without it)'
  'hyprsunset: the Night light tile (dimmed "No hyprsunset" without it)'
  "omamobile-settings: Omarchy Mobile's Settings app (independent of the shell; the image installs it)"
  'gum: the interactive chooser of omamobile-set-pin (falls back to passwd otherwise)'
  'foot: a terminal for omamobile-launch cmd and the agent prompt (any xdg-terminal-exec works)'
)
checkdepends=(nodejs diffutils patch python python-dbus python-gobject jq util-linux)
install=omamobile-shell.install

_commit=c4623572be1c141d602cf99a83ae0bf9e3eea09c
_tarball="omamobile-${_commit:0:7}.tar.gz"
_dir="omamobile-${_commit}/packages/omamobile-shell"
_patches=(
  0001-tablet-quick-settings-tiles.patch
  0002-tablet-wifi-wpa2-without-sae.patch
  0003-tablet-quiet-pollers.patch
  0004-tablet-phone-leftovers.patch
  0005-tablet-rotate-tile.patch
  0006-tablet-airplane-and-hotspot.patch
  0007-tablet-set-pin.patch
  0008-tablet-back-gesture.patch
  0009-tablet-sdcard-tile.patch
  0010-tablet-modem.patch
  0011-tablet-mobile-settings.patch
  0012-tablet-modem-tile.patch
  0013-tablet-call-card.patch
)
source=(
  "${_tarball}::${url}/archive/${_commit}.tar.gz"
  omamobile-shell.install
  tablet-shell.json
  tablet-home.json
  "${_patches[@]}"
)
noextract=("${_tarball}")
sha256sums=(
  'b6a572de8b1e29b79d5c29165d70f683564f5a6908de1a055c824579da1b37a6'
  'SKIP'
  'SKIP'
  'SKIP'
  'SKIP'
  'SKIP'
